      "section_number": "9.7.8",
      "section_heading": "Logic and Shift Instructions",
      "html_anchor": "logic-and-shift-instructions",
      "html_line_start": 14236,
      "html_line_end": 14255,
      "exact_quote": "The logic and shift instructions are fundamentally untyped, performing bit-wise operations on operands of any type, provided the operands are of the same size. This permits bit-wise operations on floating point values without having to define a union to access the bits.",
      "local_source_path": "documents/sources/nvidia/ptx/9.3/raw/ptx_isa_9.3.html",
      "source_sha256": "e2095c4ae00fe81fa18325b8e26c4a41b94965295c7affd7ff7f787fd98a8856",
      "fragment_sha256": "NOT_COMPUTED",
      "reason_for_inclusion": "Family-level semantics/context for logic/shift instruction bitwise behavior and same-size requirement."
    },
    {
      "fragment_id": "PTX-9.3-ORB16-009",
      "document_id": "ptx-isa-9.3-html",
      "publisher": "NVIDIA Corporation",
      "specification_version": "9.3",
      "source_kind": "HTML",
      "section_number": "5.2.1",
      "section_heading": "Fundamental Types",
      "html_anchor": "fundamental-types",
      "html_line_start": 3015,
      "html_line_end": 3019,
      "exact_quote": "In PTX, the fundamental types reflect the native data types supported by the target architectures. A fundamental type specifies both a basic type and a size.",
      "local_source_path": "documents/sources/nvidia/ptx/9.3/raw/ptx_isa_9.3.html",
      "source_sha256": "e2095c4ae00fe81fa18325b8e26c4a41b94965295c7affd7ff7f787fd98a8856",
      "fragment_sha256": "NOT_COMPUTED",
      "reason_for_inclusion": "Background on types and that instruction/type specifiers denote size and base type."
    },
    {
      "fragment_id": "PTX-9.3-ORB16-010",
      "document_id": "ptx-isa-9.3-html",
      "publisher": "NVIDIA Corporation",
      "specification_version": "9.3",
      "source_kind": "HTML",
      "section_number": "5.2.1",
      "section_heading": "Fundamental Types",
      "html_anchor": "fundamental-types-fundamental-type-specifiers",
      "html_line_start": 3053,
      "html_line_end": 3059,
      "exact_quote": "Bits (untyped): .b8, .b16, .b32, .b64, .b128",
      "local_source_path": "documents/sources/nvidia/ptx/9.3/raw/ptx_isa_9.3.html",
      "source_sha256": "e2095c4ae00fe81fa18325b8e26c4a41b94965295c7affd7ff7f787fd98a8856",
      "fragment_sha256": "NOT_COMPUTED",
      "reason_for_inclusion": "Defines .b16 as a fundamental bit-size specifier."
    },
    {
      "fragment_id": "PTX-9.3-ORB16-011",
      "document_id": "ptx-isa-9.3-html",
      "publisher": "NVIDIA Corporation",
      "specification_version": "9.3",
      "source_kind": "HTML",
      "section_number": "5.2.1",
      "section_heading": "Fundamental Types",
      "html_anchor": "fundamental-types",
      "html_line_start": 3062,
      "html_line_end": 3066,
      "exact_quote": "Most instructions have one or more type specifiers, needed to fully specify instruction behavior. Operand types and sizes are checked against instruction types for compatibility.\nTwo fundamental types are compatible if they have the same basic type and are the same size. Signed and unsigned integer types are compatible if they have the same size. The bit-size type is compatible with any fundamental type having the same size.",
      "local_source_path": "documents/sources/nvidia/ptx/9.3/raw/ptx_isa_9.3.html",
      "source_sha256": "e2095c4ae00fe81fa18325b8e26c4a41b94965295c7affd7ff7f787fd98a8856",
      "fragment_sha256": "NOT_COMPUTED",
      "reason_for_inclusion": "Compatibility framework and operand-size checking rules referenced in notes for or."
    },
    {
      "fragment_id": "PTX-9.3-ORB16-012",
      "document_id": "ptx-isa-9.3-html",
      "publisher": "NVIDIA Corporation",
      "specification_version": "9.3",
      "source_kind": "HTML",
      "section_number": "9.2",
      "section_heading": "PTX Instructions",
      "html_anchor": "ptx-instructions",
      "html_line_start": 7513,
      "html_line_end": 7527,
      "exact_quote": "PTX instructions generally have from zero to four operands, plus an optional guard predicate appearing after an @ symbol to the left of the opcode:\n@p opcode;\n@p opcode a;\n@p opcode d, a;\n@p opcode d, a, b;\n@p opcode d, a, b, c;\nFor instructions that create a result value, the d operand is the destination operand, while a, b, and c are source operands.",
      "local_source_path": "documents/sources/nvidia/ptx/9.3/raw/ptx_isa_9.3.html",
      "source_sha256": "e2095c4ae00fe81fa18325b8e26c4a41b94965295c7affd7ff7f787fd98a8856",
      "fragment_sha256": "NOT_COMPUTED",
      "reason_for_inclusion": "Operand ordering and optional guard predicate syntax for @, directly applicable to or.b16's 3-operand form."
    },
    {
      "fragment_id": "PTX-9.3-ORB16-013",
      "document_id": "ptx-isa-9.3-html",
      "publisher": "NVIDIA Corporation",
      "specification_version": "9.3",
      "source_kind": "HTML",
      "section_number": "9.7.13.2",
      "section_heading": "Control Flow Instructions: @",
      "html_anchor": "control-flow-instructions-at",
      "html_line_start": 21826,
      "html_line_end": 21841,
      "exact_quote": "Execute an instruction or instruction block for threads that have the guard predicate True. Threads with a False guard predicate do nothing.",
      "local_source_path": "documents/sources/nvidia/ptx/9.3/raw/ptx_isa_9.3.html",
      "source_sha256": "e2095c4ae00fe81fa18325b8e26c4a41b94965295c7affd7ff7f787fd98a8856",
      "fragment_sha256": "NOT_COMPUTED",
      "reason_for_inclusion": "Explicit false-guard behavior for predicate guards used by all instructions that use guard predicates."
    },
    {
      "fragment_id": "PTX-9.3-ORB16-014",
      "document_id": "ptx-isa-9.3-html",
      "publisher": "NVIDIA Corporation",
      "specification_version": "9.3",
      "source_kind": "HTML",
      "section_number": "9.7.13.2",
      "section_heading": "Control Flow Instructions: @",
      "html_anchor": "control-flow-instructions-at",
      "html_line_start": 21840,
      "html_line_end": 21842,
      "exact_quote": "If {!}p then instruction",
      "local_source_path": "documents/sources/nvidia/ptx/9.3/raw/ptx_isa_9.3.html",
      "source_sha256": "e2095c4ae00fe81fa18325b8e26c4a41b94965295c7affd7ff7f787fd98a8856",
      "fragment_sha256": "NOT_COMPUTED",
