    },
    {
      "fragment_id": "PTX-9.3-ORB16-015",
      "document_id": "ptx-isa-9.3-html",
      "publisher": "NVIDIA Corporation",
      "specification_version": "9.3",
      "source_kind": "HTML",
      "section_number": "9.3",
      "section_heading": "Predicated Execution",
      "html_anchor": "predicated-execution",
      "html_line_start": 7537,
      "html_line_end": 7550,
      "exact_quote": "In PTX, predicate registers are virtual and have .pred as the type specifier. So, predicate registers can be declared as\n.reg .pred p, q, r;\nAll instructions have an optional guard predicate which controls conditional execution of the instruction",
      "local_source_path": "documents/sources/nvidia/ptx/9.3/raw/ptx_isa_9.3.html",
      "source_sha256": "e2095c4ae00fe81fa18325b8e26c4a41b94965295c7affd7ff7f787fd98a8856",
      "fragment_sha256": "NOT_COMPUTED",
      "reason_for_inclusion": "General predication guard syntax and predicate type declaration context."
